TI  - The Rise and Fall of the Forge Booth
AU  - White, William J.
T2  - Tabletop RPG Design in Theory and Practice at the Forge, 2001–2012: Designs and Discussions
A2  - White, William J.
T3  - Palgrave Games in Context
AB  - This chapter describes the history of the Forge Booth at Gen Con, an international gaming convention whose origins are intertwined with that of Dungeons & Dragons. It describes the organization of an effort by members of the Forge to help Ron Edwards sell and demonstrate his game Sorcerer in 2001, and how that effort evolved into an annual project to showcase indie games for the broader culture of TRPG gaming. It discusses the experience of Forge Booth participants, and explores some of the tensions that contributed to changes at the Forge Booth before its eventual cessation as part of the broader ‘Winter of the Forge.’
