TI  - Go Read the Threads: Communication at the Forge
AU  - White, William J.
T2  - Tabletop RPG Design in Theory and Practice at the Forge, 2001–2012: Designs and Discussions
A2  - White, William J.
T3  - Palgrave Games in Context
AB  - This chapter explores the character of communication at the Forge in more depth. It begins with an examination of the philosophy underlying the moderation practices employed by Ron Edwards at the Forge before examining the notorious ‘brain damage controversy’ that roiled the indie scene in 2006 and continued to reverberate for some time. It then turns to a discussion of ‘Actual Play’ or AP as a speech genre or type of post at the Forge, and explores AP as a mode of communication that relies on dialogue for its full effect.
