TY  - CHAP
TI  - Educational Live Action Role-playing Games: A Secondary Literature Review
AU  - Bowman, Sarah Lynne
T2  - The Wyrd Con Companion Book 2014
A2  - Bowman, Sarah Lynne
AB  - This article will cover the current literature pertaining to educational live-action role-playing games (edu-larp) and related phenomena. Though edu-larp is a rather recent development emerging from the leisure activity of role-playing games, various other spheres have emphasized the pedagogical value of role-playing as a method, including education, theatre, psychodrama, military, business, and health care. This literature review will streamline the discourse surrounding games, simulation, drama, and role-playing with the recent development of edu-larp, emphasizing the various cognitive, affective, and behavioral benefits detailed in the research. The review will also discuss the challenges faced by edu-larp designers and instructors, offering possible solutions.
