TI  - The Making of Nordic Larp: Documenting a Tradition of Ephemeral Co-Creative Play
AU  - Stenros, Jaakko
AU  - Montola, Markus
T2  - 5th International Conference on Digital Research Association: Think Design Play, DiGRA 2011
AB  - Research and documentation of live action role-playing games, or larps, must tackle problems of ephemerality, subjectivity, first person audience and co-creation, as well as the underlying question of what larps are. In this paper these challenges are outlined and solutions to handling them are proposed. This is done through the prism of producing a picture-heavy art book on Nordic larp. The paper also discussed the problems of writing about game cultures as an insider and makes a case for addressing normative choices in game descriptions head on. © 2011 Authors & Digital Games Research Association DiGRA.
