TI  - FurScience! A summary of five years of research from the International Anthropomorphic Research Project
AU  - Plante, Courtney
AU  - Reysen, Stephen
AU  - Roberts, Sharon E.
AU  - Gerbasi, Kathleen
AB  - The International Anthropomorphic Research Project is a group of social scientists conducting research to gain a better understanding of the furry fandom. In the present book we present the main findings from a variety of studies, including more than 10,000 furry participants, over the past five years. The book seeks to answer questions often asked about furries, such as what is a furry? Do furries really think they’re animals? Is it true that all furries where fursuits? Whether you’ve never heard of furries before or you’ve been a furry for decades, you’re sure to learn something from this book. 

