TI  - Beauty in Larp
AU  - Stenros, Jaakko
AU  - MacDonald, James Lórien
T2  - What Do We Do When We Play?
A2  - Saitta, Eleanor
A2  - Koljonen, Johanna
A2  - Särkijärvi, Jukka
A2  - Serup Grove, Anne
A2  - Männistö, Pauliina
A2  - Makkonen, Mia
AB  - Larp is both beautiful to see and beautiful to do. Participants can appreciate the performative excellence of individual performances and other skilful exhibitions, there is a visual surface that can be enthralling regardless of the context, and certainly there is the intricate work in crafting the rule-bound bespoke design. These elements we can appreciate from afar, as an audience, whether we are also participants, or even just someone going through larp documentation, be it design documents (larp-as-designed), photographs, video, written reflections, or costumes (larp-as-remembered).

The larp as played, for the participants, has three additional ways to encounter beauty. In larp, the participants mutually play a world into being by improvising within the rules and structures given by the design, partaking in emergent co-creation through play and inter-immersion. Furthermore, participants engage in vulnerable and generous play while being mindful, embodied, and present. Yet they also remain reflexive about the conceit of larp and strive for structural and narrative excellence.
