AB  - Despite publishing endeavours such as the Ballantine Adult Fantasy Series in the 1970s and Fantasy Masterworks in the early 2000s, the canon of modern fantasy is still very much in ﬂux. This Element examines four key questions raised by the prospect of a fantasy canon: the way in which canon and genre inﬂuence each other; the overwhelming presence of Tolkien in any discussion of the classics of fantasy; the multimedia and transmedia nature of the ﬁeld; and the push for a more inclusive and diverse canon.
