TY  - JOUR
TI  - What Fantasy Role-Playing Games Can Teach Your Children (or Even You)
AU  - Betz, Ulrich A. K.
T2  - British Journal of Educational Technology
AB  - With the holiday season closing in and some time to relax at hand, some of us see our children or even ourselves occasionally zoom in to one of the fantasy role-playing games that beam the player into a parallel world of adventure, such as the Dungeons & Dragons series (invented by Gary Gygax and Dave Arneson in 1974), Ultima or Wizardry, to name a few of the classics of this genre (Fine, 1983). In a typical setting, a party of skilled adventurers engages on a dungeon crawl aligned along a common goal to beat the competition and to find and uncover enormous riches that wait out there—sounds familiar, you mean, to your daily work in business or R&D? Well, I can tell you that the similarities do not end here, and there are many eternal business and management principles hidden in the daily life of an adventuring party!
