TY  - JOUR
TI  - The Folklore of Roleplaying
AU  - Bloy, Michael
AB  - In the roleplaying hobby , gamers create worlds and populate them with characters. Often, these worlds and these characters are based, either consciously or unconsciously , on mythic or legendary themes. Roleplaying is, along with religious services and campfire ghost stories, the closest this society comes to storytelling in the sense of a few people clustered around the fire swapping stories. Roleplaying has also evolved its own special set of superstitions, myths, and folklore. Most of this is superstition related to dice and the other materials of gaming, mixed in with a collection of popular culture references.
