TY  - BOOK
TI  - Heroic Worlds: A History and Guide to Role-Playing Games
AU  - Schick, Lawrence
AB  - The thousands of games and game systems described in this volume show that role-playing games have gained considerable popularity since the first appearance of Dungeons and Dragons in 1974. Schick, a succesful game designer himself, succinctly defines these paper or "table-top" games as "quantified interactive storytelling." The reference guide proper is preceded by two informative sections, "What is a Role-Playing Game?" and "The History of Role-Playing Games." The game descriptions are divided into 22 genres (and subgenres), and include fantasy (by far the most numerous), science fiction, comic book superheroes, espionage, and westerns. Each section begins with a brief descriptive overview and Schick's list of recommended games for that genre. Entries are also interspersed with brief essays and comments from designers concerning their games and their ideas about role-playing games in general. The game descriptions are supplemented by a directory of game publishers, a list of award-winning games, definitions of terms, a timeline, and a title index. Although very well written and well organized, this work is not a needed addition for most academic libraries, being recommended only for strong popular culture or games and recreation collections. --R. Nash, University of Nebraska at Omaha Copyright 1992 American Library Association
