TI  - Adventures in Gaming Therapy
AU  - Davis, Adam
AU  - Johns, Adam
AB  - This panel about the use of RPGs to improve social skills was presented at PAX South 2016. It features Adam Davis and Adam Johns of Wheelhouse Workshop, a Seattle area organization which uses role playing games like Dungeons and Dragons to help their teenage clients become more confident, creative, and socially capable.

Panel Description:

Please Don't Punch the GM: Adventures in Gaming Therapy

Games like Dungeons and Dragons are often regarded by pop culture as nerdy and antisocial, but Wheelhouse Workshop founders Adam Davis and Adam Johns use them to help their neurodiverse teen clients become more confident and socially capable. Come hear how these lifelong gamers used their training in counseling, drama therapy, and human development to embark on a new frontier in therapy, ask questions about your own gaming experience, and celebrate how the games we love are more than just games.
