TY  - THES
TI  - Therapy & Dragons: A look into the Possible Applications of Table Top Role Playing Games in Therapy with Adolescents
AU  - Gutierrez, Raul
AB  - The purpose of this study was to gain a better understanding on the use of Table Top Role Playing Games (TRPGs) in therapy with adolescents. This qualitative study utilized individual interviews as a means to extract themes from mental health practitioners who have provided this intervention with their clients in an individual/group therapy setting. Results were transcribed to written form. Qualitative analysis procedures were followed to identify themes and subthemes. Areas of particular interest to the social work profession were: applicability to clients of any age, the client-tailored narrative, use of TRPGs in a group setting, TRPGs as a form of exposure therapy. Possible risks of utilizing this intervention and limitations of the study were also introduced.
