TY  - JOUR
TI  - Sign: A Case Study in Learning the Philosophy of Language through Games
AU  - Willard, Mary Beth
T2  - Teaching Philosophy
AB  - I present a case study of the use of a table-top role-playing game in a mid-level course that presupposes no previous familiarity with philosophy. The course covered philosophical analyses of propaganda and language, and the pedagogical purpose of the game was to help students grasp the basics of philosophical and linguistic theories of assertion quickly. The game, Sign, directs players to create a signed language collaboratively, and thus forces them to pay attention to the subtle ways in which communication occurs.
