TI  - Tabletop Roleplaying Games as Emotional Resiliency Factor
AU  - Taylor, Glen R.
AB  - This study used an Internet-distributed survey to assess the relationship between play of tabletop roleplaying games (TRPGs) and current general emotional well-being, in order to assess whether TRPGs may be considered to promote emotional resiliency and protect against emotional distress in adult participants. The survey included questions about demographics, TRPG experience, and four aspects of emotional distress (depression, anxiety, social isolation, and addictive behaviors) to test the hypothesis that having played TRPGs extensively or recently was negatively correlated with general emotional distress and each of the four aspects.
