TI  - Metagaming in Tabletop Role-Playing Games
AU  - Lickteig, Seth J.
T2  - PhD&D Journal
AB  - This article explores the phenomenon of metagaming as it occurs in tabletop role-playing games. A preliminary literature review into the phrase metagaming yields the foundational for defining the various aspects of what metagaming has come to encompass. Utilizing the work of Carter, Gibbs, and Harrop (2012) multiple meanings of metagaming are clarified and elaborated upon. The author posits the development of two unique facets of metagaming within tabletop role-playing games: mechanical and narrative metagaming. It concludes with a discussion on the morality of utilizing metagaming processes during gameplay.
