TI  - Roll for Initiative: A Librarian’s Primer for Collecting Tabletop Role-Playing Games
AU  - Forsythe, Carlie
T2  - Emerging Library & Information Perspectives
AB  - Tabletop role-playing games originated in the 1970s with the introduction of the popular role-playing game, Dungeons & Dragons. Today, tabletop role-playing games make for valuable investments in libraries as they are effective tools for providing rich environments for learning and developing a variety of social and technical skills. This paper largely focuses on collecting tabletop role-playing games in libraries, as well as provides an introduction to role-playing games, their systems and mechanics, and how games are published.
