TY  - THES
TI  - Roll for Identity: A Study of Tabletop Roleplaying Games and Exploring Identity
AU  - Shepherd, Toriana
AB  - This work seeks to understand the use of tabletop roleplaying games such as Dungeons and Dragons in understanding and exploring identity. Using a methodology based in narrative empathy and a theoretical framework of queer theory, narrative empathy, and adaptation theory among others, this thesis identifies how the game’s character creation process and full autonomy of the player character within the confines of the game allow for individuals to use the game to explore identities. Through ethnographic research with queer identifying individuals, the author explores the use of Dungeons and Dragons by the research participants in the exploration of individual identities both personal and other.
