TY  - THES
TI  - Tabletop Role-Playing Games Simulator with Procedurally Generated 2D Dungeon Levels
AU  - Wyrostkiewicz, Aleksandra
AB  - Tabletop Role-Playing Game is a form of an asymmetrical role-playing game, where participants incarnate in the characters and act out their role, describing their actions through speech. While voice can be enough of a tool for the simplest games, additional ones are usually used for visualization of encounters or for dungeon crawling. This thesis demonstrates a Virtual Tabletop program, which is a game helper tool for preparing and playing tabletop role-playing games. It consists of a procedural generator of dungeon levels, a level editor, and a level play-through simulator. The procedural generation is using modified Space Partitioning Algorithm and Cellular Automaton for two types of dungeon levels, mansion-like and cavern-like respectively. This work also includes an analysis of the most common procedural map generation methods and their usage in game development, as procedural content generation is an increasingly popular way of cutting down costs and development time, while keeping the content original and interesting.
