AB  - Interactive narrative systems are often embedded in games: works of playable media that enable players to participate in or experience a story through game mechanics. But play practices directed toward the expressive creation of story seem to challenge a games-centric understanding of narrative play. Consequently, we propose that some interactive narrative systems can be better understood as a diﬀerent form of playable media: narrative instruments, analogous to musical instruments in their provision of support for authorship-oriented forms of play.
