TI  - Ripple: A Role-Playing Game (RPG) that Shifts Power Dynamics in Healthcare
AU  - Burgas, Kim
AU  - Yanamandala, Hrudaya Veena
T3  - PDC '22
AB  - Ripple invites participants into a role-playing game (RPG) to shift traditional power dynamics seen within healthcare systems in the United States and to unpack ‘intangible’ non-clinical needs that aren't easily communicated or identified even with participatory approaches. Through this RPG, participants will explore fictional worlds and scenarios through three acts: 1. exploring oneself through individual character building, 2. exploring the relationships of those in the community of individuals, 3. navigating scenarios and storytelling together. As a prototype Ripple will help to understand the value of RPGs in participatory design and to understand the ‘invisible’ needs beyond treatment needs in a cancer patient and their caregivers’ journey.
