TY  - JOUR
TI  - 5,000 Years of Storytelling: Dungeons & Dragons as a lens of analysis for The Epic of Gilgamesh
AU  - Kychenthal, Skye
AB  - Despite the epic’s authorship likely being 5,000 years ago, The Epic of Gilgamesh’s methods of storytelling, and the way it introduces one of the main characters – Enkidu – is incredibly similar to the modern oral tradition of storytelling that is Dungeons & Dragons. This leads the game of Dungeons & Dragons to be an optimal lens of analysis for the question Enkidu’s creation poses: specifically the question of virtue in civilization versus the wilderness. The purpose of this paper is to do a close reading of lines I.94 to I.133 of the 2003 Penguin Books translation of The Epic of Gilgamesh to substantiate the validity of using Dungeons & Dragons for a framework of analysis.
