AB  - Low student participation in the classroom is a concern for teachers. This is a problem with no territory, no boundaries, and no date for an end. It is an irrepressible reality that the traditional school must face. In this context, the present study brings a proposal for the development of skills and knowledge in Portuguese language through RPG, a tool that involves: socialization, cooperation, creativity, interactivity, and interdisciplinarity. As a practical example, the work also evaluates for such purpose the work "A Bandeira do Elefante e da Arara - Livro de interpretação de papéis", a national RPG, inspired by Brazilian fantasy books, written by Christopher Kastensmidt (2017). This is a theoretical study, the application and evaluation of the efficiency and effectiveness of the method in the classroom may be a later distinct research.
