TI  - Climate Larps: Environmental Design in Nordic Larp
AU  - op de Beke, Laura
T2  - Analog Game Studies
AB  - Another essay on how form and content relate to each other is Laura op de Beke’s “Climate Larps: Environmental Design in Nordic Larp.” Here, we see both op de Beke’s design interventions in the environmental discourse with a game called Leviathan, which has players navigate a steadily-changing landscape and set of resources, as well as the many other forms of environmental engagement in the Nordic larp community. This essay is an invitation for others to critically assess their own climate-change game designs, as well as see themselves in vibrant dialogue with many others. There is, after all, no single way to represent hyper-objects such as climate change and ecological crisis.
