TY  - THES
TI  - Worldbuilding on RPG Open Worlds
AU  - Vázquez Porcar, Pol
AB  - Creating a world can be tricky and confusing, even overwhelming when we decide to start creating a fantasy world. There’s a lot of depth and complexity when creating a fantasy world, and starting blank can turn very fast into a frustrating, never ending process. This project analyzes a lot of different authors and games to resolve this topic: how can we make creating a fantasy world easier and accessible for newbies? Our objective is to find the most important things to look for when creating one, things that we should avoid and things that we should probably add. We will take a look into a lot of open-world games that deal with the same problem as some TTRPGs and RPGs: the impossibility to know what the players will do next. We will see how they manage their races, the creation of cities and kingdoms, entire pantheons of deities and magic systems that feel integrated to the world. To accomplish that, we will make an extensive research synthesis of narrative, open world games, fantasy and worldbuilding and explore the current state of these topics regarding our topic, including an analysis of 5 open world games
