TI  - From Suspension of Disbelief to Production of Belief: The Case of Alternate Reality Games
AU  - Jagoda, Patrick
T2  - The Routledge Handbook of Fiction and Belief
A2  - James, Alison
A2  - Kubo, Akihiro
A2  - Lavocat, Françoise
AB  - This chapter explores a limit case of fictional realities: the Alternate Reality Game (ARG). ARGs are narrative-driven experiences that include interactive challenges across online and offline settings. They draw on elements of Live Action Roleplaying Games and Method acting without replicating either. ARGs are characterized by a “This Is Not a Game” aesthetic that blurs fiction and reality. Unlike literary or cinematic works of fiction, which engage in a suspension of disbelief, ARGs facilitate a production of belief. They can teach us about fictionality in the twenty-first century and contemporary “post-truth” politics and “fake news” that result from algorithmic bias.
