AB  - This chapter surveys documented role-play, from after-battle reports in wargaming to Actual Play reports of tabletop RPG sessions on online forums, Let’s Plays of digital RPGs, documented larp, and today’s highly popular tabletop RPG sessions distributed online as video streams or podcasts, like Acquisitions Incorporated, Critical Role, or Role-Playing Public Radio. The chapter teases out characteristics of documented play such as performance for an audience and interacting with a viewership. And it unpacks how the success of popular Actual Play franchises has helped role-playing games go mainstream as well as the complexities and issues of commercializing a hobby activity.
