TI  - An Elegant Little Instrument: The Japanese Standards Association and the Birth of the Modern d20
AU  - Evan, Peter D.
T2  - Analog Game Studies
AB  - First, Peter D. Evan rolls a critical hit with their essay “An Elegant Little Instrument: The Japanese Standards Association and the Birth of the Modern d20,” which excavates the modern history and near predominance of the twenty-sided die. Evan’s genealogy of the d20 uncovers a fascinating tale that spans three decades and across Asia, Europe, and North America, beginning with the Japanese Standards Association in the 1950s and ending with the Bristol Wargames Society and TSR in the 1970s.
