TI  - Board and Video Games: Mythical Gateways Towards English
AU  - Stiegelbauer, Laura Rebeca
AU  - Diaconescu, Marilena
T2  - Dimensiuni ale educației moderne : Realități și perspective
AB  - Game education, at its core, in addition to influencing the formation of children and teenagers, facilitating healthy growth, permanent enrichment, is part of the most uplifting spirit of democratic practice while investing in a serious production of knowledge. In this sense, it can be understood that pedagogical games can be a link between didactic practice and the success of the teaching and learning process, by providing creativity and interaction, as well as awakening the student’s interest and understanding, connecting their reality with the reality presented and lived in the English language classroom. Teachers' and students’ relation is transformed into a more dynamic activity, sharpening the latter’s curiosity and promoting knowledge. Although teachers are aware of the importance and efficiency of games as pedagogical resources, they rarely use them, especially during English classes. It is extremely important to introduce game activities in schools. These activities have the power to facilitate both the progress of the student’s integral personality and the progress of each of his psychological, intellectual and moral functions. In addition, lucidity not only influences children, but also brings several benefits to adults, who love to learn something while having fun. Thus, the importance of play in the school context is perceived, providing greater interaction between students and their learning, making content more attractive and meaningful, from the students’ perspective.
