TY  - THES
TI  - Dungeons & Dragons Game Support Application
AU  - Štalmach, Martin
AB  - This thesis aims to design and implement a cross-platform desktop and mobile application, mainly for Windows and Android platforms, that players could use while playing the tabletop role-playing game Dungeons & Dragons. The idea is to abstract physical data so the players can keep track of their game progress in digital form. The theoretical part consists of exploring currently available applications for players of fantasy tabletop role-playing games, with the main focus being the game Dungeons & Dragons, analyzing them, and establishing the desired functionality of the new application. The theoretical part also includes proper system analysis and design. The practical part is the implementation of the application itself.
