TI  - Preface
AU  - Peterson, Jon
T2  - Playing at the World, 2E: The Invention of Dungeons & Dragons
AB  - Near the beginning of this book, I refer to the original 1974 Dungeons & Dragons as a work "printed in miniscule numbers by determined amateurs, distributed with little fanfare, and slated to reach only a tiny community of interest before an almost certain plummet into utter obscurity." Roughly the same could be said about the 2012 book Playing at the World: a 700-page print-on-demand work that I began writing around 2007. It aimed to show the cultural and conceptual roots of the game design principles that D&D popularized: everything from dungeons and dragons to experience points and levels, hit points and armor class, referees (dungeon masters) and players, monsters and treasure, dice and maps. A bit of poking around convinced me that there was an untold story there, and I could see a path to telling it.
