AB  - Early in 1974, a company in Lake Geneva, Wisconsin, called Tactical Studies Rules released the game Dungeons & Dragons. The product consisted of three slim booklets and a few reference sheets housed in a woodgrain- patterned cardboard box. The authors are identified on the cover as "Gygax & Arneson." The only hint its exterior gives to the subject of the game is this legend: "Rules for Fantastic Medieval Wargames Campaigns Playable with Paper and Pencil and Miniature Figures."
