AB  - The Siege of Bodenburg is a miniature wargame in the medieval setting, and thus an ancestor of "Fantastic Medieval Wargames Campaigns."1 Its scenario involves the fictitious stronghold of a German "Count von Boden," an imaginary ancestor of the designer, Henry Bodenstedt. A horde of Huns and Turks with siege engines assault the town and face a garrison armed with swords, bows, and other medieval implements. Bodenstedt assigned no specific date or place to the game, and most likely, as Wagner observed above, the scenario of The Siege of Bodenburg owes more to the miniatures stocked by Continental Hobby Supplies than any inspirational historical incident.
