AB  - If all that has been recounted so far served only to explicate "medieval wargames," now we can begin to investigate "fantastic medieval wargames." Chainmail included a "Fantasy Supplement" that allowed wargamers to "refight the epic struggles related by J. R. R. Tolkien, Robert E. Howard, and other fantasy writers; or you can devise your own 'world', and conduct fantastic campaigns and conflicts based on it."1 Why attach these rules to Chainmail? Because "most of the fantastic battles related in novels more closely resemble medieval warfare than they do earlier or later forms of combat."
