TI  - 11 Blackmoor
AU  - Peterson, Jon
T2  - Playing at the World, 2E: The Invention of Dungeons & Dragons
AB  - In the spring of 1971, Arneson faced an internal political challenge within his Twin Cities wargaming group: Randy Hoffa, who did not care for Arneson's playstyle and campaign administration, persuaded the club to endorse a rival Napoleonic campaign. The April Corner of the Table proclaimed the "elimination of the office of strategic referee," though not without an expression of "gratitude and appreciation to Dave Arneson" (COTT 3 (4), 1971). Arneson insisted that the "vaunted Hoffa campaign" was "not viable and indeed probably will never start," a belief that history would vindicate; but for the moment, his own Napoleonic Simulation Campaign stalled (COTT May 1971 Supplement).
