TI  - 17 Dungeons & Dragons in Los Angeles Fandom
AU  - Peterson, Jon
T2  - Playing at the World, 2E: The Invention of Dungeons & Dragons
AB  - Gygax carefully supervised and encouraged the spread of Dungeons & Dragons throughout the wargaming community in the Midwest, but the game's wild propagation through science-fiction fandom rode a wave of sheer grassroots advocacy. Once the Twin Cities gamers had offhandedly sparked the interest of Minn-stf, the highly interconnected national community of science-fiction fans created many opportunities for crosspollination: in amateur press associations (APAs), at large-scale science-fiction conventions, and through the multitude of college-aged fans who commuted between their hometowns and distant universities. Just as VanGrasstek brought his Dungeon to the World Science Fiction Convention, so too did other members of Minneapolis fandom bring the game to the attention of distant venues.
