TI  - 23 Cooperate or Compete?
AU  - Peterson, Jon
T2  - Playing at the World, 2E: The Invention of Dungeons & Dragons
AB  - In July 1976, two enthusiasts from Illinois named Bob Bledsaw and Bill Owen arranged a meeting at TSR in Lake Geneva. Owen had developed a set of American Civil War rules, and TSR remained sincerely interested in publishing traditional board and miniature wargame systems. Upon their arrival, they met with some of the core design team, including Dave Arneson. Secretly, in addition to the Civil War rules, Bledsaw and Owen had smuggled in a wealth of material from Bledsaw's sprawling Dungeons & Dragons campaign.
