TI  - 24 d&d among the rpgs
AU  - Peterson, Jon
T2  - Playing at the World, 2E: The Invention of Dungeons & Dragons
AB  - Such were the starting conditions of the role-playing game industry. A growing community of fans adored Dungeons & Dragons, wanting both to contribute to the game and to take its innovations in new directions— not necessarily with TSR's blessing. And then there was TSR itself, a fledgling company that had sold around four thousand copies of D&D by the beginning of 1976, and in the twelve months that followed, would sell around twice that number. Over the course of that year, TSR slowly pivoted to embrace the term "role-playing game" for its marquee products—a decision made necessary by the whim of the community at large, which had located D&D within that genre—but also motivated by how poorly verbiage like "fantastic medieval wargames campaigns" would apply to the releases in its pipeline.
