TY  - ICOMM
TI  - Dave Arneson questions and JG too...
AU  - Fisher, Robert
AB  - « To the limited view of this outsider, you can draw a line from Braunstein to Blackmoor to Greyhawk to D&D. Not only do I think Arneson doesn't get as much respect & credit as he deserves, I think Dave Wesely gets almost none of the credit he deserves.

While Gygax gets more respect & credit, I've come to believe he deserves even more credit than most people give him.

& there are many other people whose contributions were invaluable. Some names we know: Rob Kuntz, Jim Ward, Steve Marsh, Frank Mentzer, Tom Moldvay, Law Shick, &c., &c. How many are there whose names we don't know? We only have the names printed on the books & anecdotes to go by.

& that's not even going far from of LG. Bob Bledsoe, Paul Jacquays, Marc W. Miller, Frank Chadwick, Steve Perrin, Greg Stafford, &c, &c.

Anyway, I suppose if there's a point my rambling it's that D&D & the hobby have required a lot of different talents & there's a lot of people with different talents that made it happen. EGG's & DA's names were on it. Comparing their contributions are comparing apples & oranges. They both deserve boatloads of credit for their individual talents as do a couple boatloads of other people.»
