TI  - AI generated tabletop roleplaying game for communal Sámi storytelling
AU  - Roby-Tomić, Ernie
AU  - Valkeapää, Samuel
AU  - Somby, Ánde
AU  - Pedersen, Bjørn-Richard
AU  - Bongo, Lars Ailo
AB  - The democratization of AI offers new opportunities for indigenous people to tell their stories. However, current generative AI models do not represent indigenous people and other minorities well. We are developing a Tabletop Roleplaying Game (TTRPG) to explore the potential and limitations of generative AI for communal storytelling for the indigenous Sámi people. Our aim is to provide a platform that can be used to create roleplaying sessions for both traditional stories and discussion of current Sámi issues. We use a custom LoRA model to generate Sámi images for the game, and ChatGPT to develop rulesets for the game, generate guides and scenario texts, and for writing custom system builder code. We are currently playtesting the game. We believe this work can be adapted for storytelling in other indigenous people and other monitories, and to make teaching material for indigenous languages and cultures.
