TY  - JOUR
TI  - Two Can Play at This Game: A Dual-Individuation Account of Games
AU  - Lee, James
T2  - Synthese
AB  - This paper defends a theory of how it is that games are identical both at a time and over time. I argue that this view is an improvement over the account that Michael Ridge defends in his paper “Individuating Games”. This improvement involves a distinction between two kinds of individuation: constitutive individuation and relational individuation. I argue that this distinction does a better job at solving the various puzzles that are related to the synchronic and diachronic identity of games. I go on to show how this approach can be applied to other social entities.
