TY  - CONF
TI  - Gamification Model for the Affective Commitment of the Technology Team in a Financial Institution
AU  - Farías-Güich, Daniel-Antonio
AU  - Rodriguez, Ciro
T2  - 2024 IEEE 16th International Conference on Computational Intelligence and Communication Networks (CICN)
AB  - This research explores the application of a gamification model as a tool to reduce the deficit in affective commitment within an IT Squad from the Technology Tribe of a financial entity in Lima, Peru. Issues negatively impacting the team's performance were identified, such as lack of communication, interpersonal conflicts, and lack of recognition, among others. The gamification model proposed in this research was designed with the aim of increasing motivation, improving interpersonal relationships, and fostering more effective collaboration, based on theories about gamification models and organizational commitment, as well as using role-playing games as a tool to develop social skills. The results of the research showed a 25% increase in the affective commitment of the IT Squad, concluding that the application of a gamification model is a viable strategy to improve the performance of IT workers.
