AB  - Dimension 20: Mice & Murder (2021) is a whodunit actual play gamemastered by Brennan Lee Mulligan and produced with a cast of comedians from Dropout, an original programming streaming service.1 Like many actual play shows that were created during the pandemic, Mice & Murder features players streaming from their homes, while Mulligan plays in the Dimension 20 (2018–) set, affectionately called the Dome. The series follows the Sylvan Sleuths, an unlikely group of animal investigators, characters who were inspired by a hodgepodge of source texts such as Sherlock Holmes, Redwall (1986), Wind in the Willows (1908), and others.2 Through the ten-episode series, the party attempts to unravel the mystery surrounding the murder of Squire Brockhollow. As the group investigates, uncovering secrets about the Squire's past as well as their own, it becomes clear that they are all in danger and must solve the mystery before it is too late.
