TY  - CONF
TI  - You Die, Then What? Engaging with Mortality in Collaborative Fantasy Narratives
AU  - Holste, Pia
T3  - Symposium 2023 in Magdeburg
AB  - This paper compares the philosophies of death embodied by death deities from
three successful fantasy series with each other through Derrida’s and Tolkien’s
notions of death as a gift. Hades in Percy Jackson (2005–2009, 2023–
present), the Raven Queen in Critical Role: Vox Machina (2015–2017),
and the Many-Faced God in A Song of Ice and Fire (1996–present) all
take on various forms, making their true essence a secret. Death can therefore
never be fully known. It is fearsome, but also connected to mercy and change.
While death is portrayed as inevitable, its finality as well as the deities’ impar-
tiality are questioned to varying degrees.
