TY  - JOUR
TI  - Markets And Merchants: A Tabletop Role-Playing Game For The Marketing Classroom
AU  - Bender, Mark
T2  - Marketing Education Review
AB  - Markets and Merchants is a teaching innovation that gamifies short decision-oriented case study discussions by augmenting them with tabletop role-playing game (TTRPG) mechanics. TTRPGs, such as Dungeons & Dragons, are immersive, collaborative games where players embody unique roles, and the game’s narrative evolves within the structure of the game’s rules and dice rolls. In addition to the inherent benefits of gamification, TTRPGs have been found to enhance players’ creativity, divergent thinking, and problem-solving capabilities, build social skills, encourage teamwork, promote perspective-taking, and foster self-reflection and peer evaluation. To implement this innovation, instructors need only a short decision-oriented case, a set of dice, and a rule sheet to share with each student group. Students are either assigned to the role of Case Master (CM), the student responsible for finessing the case and assessing peers’ recommendations for risk, reward, and cost, or the role of Strategic Decision Makers (SDMs), students who collaborate to propose a recommendation to the CM. After the CM evaluates the SDMs’ proposed recommendations, dice are rolled to determine SDMs’ earned Profit Points. This innovation provides guidelines for implementation and assessment, supports the innovation with student feedback, and proposes additional TTRPG mechanisms that may enhance gameplay and learning.
