TY  - SLIDE
TI  - Divination: Applying Retrieval-Augmented Generation with LLMs to generate content for D&D
A2  - Costa da Silva, Luiz Carlos
A2  - Renato Cordeiro, Ferreira
AB  - The Divination project provides an appli-
cation that uses the fantasy tabletop role-
playing game Dungeons and Dragons (D&D)
sourcebooks to help DMs manage players’
adventures.
The system is divided into a front-end and a
back-end. The front-end uses the Vue3js fra-
mework to provide a user chat interface, and
the back-end uses Python+FASTAPI powered
by ChatGPT-4o LLM.
To answer the questions as faithfully as
possible, avoiding LLM Hallucinations, the
back-end uses Retrieval-Augmented Genera-
tion (RAG) as a structure; this structure reads
external data from the D&D Free Rules (2024)
page and stores it on a Vector Store Database.
When a query is received in the back-end, the
RAG retrieves the most relevant chunks from
the vector store and sends them to the rest of
the system to use as context to give the most
accurate answer to the user [2]
