TY  - JOUR
TI  - Monster manuals, Nat 20s, and expression: serious leisure as portrayed in Dungeons and Dragons
AU  - Messina, Emily
T2  - Leisure Studies
AB  - Serious leisure has been characterised by perseverance, significant effort, and identification with the activity. Dungeons and Dragons (D&D), the popular tabletop role-playing game, involves long-term commitment to one’s gaming party as well as their character, in some cases developed and refined over months or years. However, little research exists examining D&D as serious leisure. The current study aims to determine what elements of Stebbins’ serious leisure qualities are present in D&D, whether Stebbins’ conceptualisations of serious leisure encompass all elements of the D&D experience as identified by focus group participants, and whether D&D experiences identified by focus group participants support alternate explanations of serious leisure. Using the Basketball/D&D winning scene (season 4, episode 1) of the Netflix show Stranger Things as stimulus material, this project conducted two focus groups using funnel pattern question delivery. Online focus groups consisting of longtime D&D players were facilitated and recorded. Transcripts from the focus groups were analysed by question, using the Constructivist Grounded Theory Method. Themes present across all questions addressed dedication, game persona, teamwork, and diversity in D&D. Most themes supported traditional conceptualisations of serious leisure, but the theme of diversity provided support for re-envisioned definitions of serious leisure.
