TY  - THES
TI  - A Translation for Live-Play D&D Content and the Merits of Tabletop Role-Playing Games
AU  - Renshaw, Holly
AB  - A game created in the 70s, Dungeons & Dragons was at times ostracized and stigmatized but is now highly popular and profitable, with millions of players across the globe. The world of Dungeons & Dragons is one where friends come together to utilize their creativity and teamwork skills to tell a collaborative story. This unique time world can enrich the lives of many, including in the untapped market of South Korea. D&D has been shown to be beneficial for social and moral development. This kind of prosocial activity can alleviate concerns about antisocial behaviors related to high internet usage in societies such as South Korea. Since D&D has yet to be popularized in South Korea, this thesis focused on how to create interest in the game by providing access to content that promotes D&D. In the Western world, a major factor in D&D’s recent success has been the development and popularity of D&D players who upload online live-streams where audiences can watch them play a real game of D&D. Creating a Korean translation for an original video using this style of content, this thesis tackles the challenge of how to adapt English language D&D content for Korean audiences, grappling with both the unique challenges of the video medium, and the major differences between the two languages.
