TY  - CHAP
TI  - Edu-larp and Positive Psychology: Theory, Practice, and Case Study
AU  - Masek, leland
T2  - Education and Analog Role-Playing Games : TeachRPG – Tabletop Role-Playing Games in the Classroom, Volume 1
A2  - Haarman, Susan
AB  - Educational live action role-playing (edu-larp) has several traditions of pedagogy, games, play, and design. Edu-larp, however, is frequently created, practiced, and developing tools outside of traditional education, play or psychological theory. This chapter will present a model of how edu-larp is a uniquely interesting tool for educating children on positive psychological content through three important educational paradigms: behaviorism, cognitivism, and constructivism. These three theoretical paradigms will be explicated through the additional use of a case study: The edu-larp program funded by the City of Tampere in Finland that has run from 2018 to present. Specific games and techniques will be used as examples for clarity. By integrating these theoretical paradigms into how they are applied in practice in a specific edu-larp program, this work hopes to extend the discourse on how academic theories of education, psychology, and play can enable a deeper understanding of designing edu-larp programs.
