TY  - CHAP
TI  - Edu-larp: The Promises and Pitfalls of the Method
AU  - Westborg, Josefin
T2  - Education and Analog Role-Playing Games
A2  - Haarman, Susan
AB  - This chapter explores the use of edu-larp (educational live action role-playing games) as a method for teaching. Instead of focusing mainly on what the method is good for, which is often the focus when discussing game-based teaching methods, this chapter takes a different approach. Based on interview data from experts working with the method, different pitfalls are highlighted, what the method might not be as good for, and what risks there are with using it. This chapter follows up with a discussion on how to mitigate some of these pitfalls and which parts are difficult to address. The purpose of this chapter is to help educators make an informed choice of when to use the method and, when they do, be able to foresee and handle problems that might arise.
