TY  - CHAP
TI  - Everybody Wins: Role-Playing Games with Students with Disabilities
AU  - Leogrande, Cathy
AU  - Brown, Aaron
T2  - Education and Analog Role-Playing Games
A2  - Haarman, Susan
AB  - This chapter describes the results of a pilot project using a teacher-adapted role-playing game in a special class with students with learning and behavioral struggles. A seven-week Harry Potter-themed Dungeons & Dragons-style game was designed to accompany the class reading of a text by the teacher candidate. Benefits included improvement in literacy, communication, problem-solving, cognitive flexibility and emotional regulation. Challenges addressed included cooperative teamwork, unpredictability of game play and impact of other classroom demands. The chapter includes review of research related to gaming and disabilities, accessibility and representation. The chapter also provides ideas for future research and practice and resources for teacher facilitation.
