TY  - JOUR
TI  - YOU are the Hero! Epic Perspectives in Dante Role-playing Games and Gamebooks
AU  - Arnaudo, Marco
T2  - Italianistica-Rivista Di Letteratura Italiana
AB  - This essay analyzes the reworking of Dante's Inferno in modern manifestations of role-play. We begin by defining role-playing gaming and showing how this activity can bring up Dante's epic elements by emphasizing action and adventure. At the same time, the interactivity of role-playing makes Dante's epic elements particularly suitable to postmodern sensibilities. The essay shows the presence of Dantean elements in the foundational game Dungeons & Dragons, starting from a 1977 game manual all the way to the most recent editions. The independent D&D adventure Inferno by Geoffry Dale is analyzed in detail as an attempt to turn Dante's work into a script for interactive play. Italian contributions of designers of role-playing games and gamebooks (a manifestation of roleplay) are analyzed in detail too, with an emphasis on their original contribution to a detailed depiction of the characters of the damned.
