T2  - International Journal of Role-Playing
AB  - This paper works to flesh out the concept of the murderhobo particularly in the tabletop game Dungeons &amp; Dragons. As a term known in the gaming world, the murderhobo has not been fully or clearly defined in game studies, though it could prove a useful topic in terms of game culture and player behavior. This paper seeks to provide an examination of the concept through a practice theory lens and relates how it could be seen in a multitude of ways in the gaming space. This investigation lays the groundwork for more purposeful discussion of the topic and its tie to game culture.
