AU  - Zajac, Victoria
AU  - Conrad, Rachael
AU  - Bean, Anthony M
T2  - Journal of Psychology and Psychotherapy Research
AB  - The therapeutic use of tabletop role-playing games (TTRPGs) has gained increasing attention in clinical, psychoeducational, and community settings. This scoping review aimed to systematically map the literature on the psychological, therapeutic, and educational applications of TTRPGs, including Dungeons & Dragons and related analog systems. Following PRISMA-ScR procedures, 73 sources were identified through database searches, citation chaining, and grey literature review, then charted for study characteristics, populations, settings, intervention targets, and reported outcomes.
