TY  - JOUR
TI  - Inspiration Points! A Creative Adventure Through the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual
AU  - Stillwell, Sarah
T2  - Journal of Creativity in Mental Health
AB  - This paper presents an innovative role-playing game (RPG)-based approach to teaching diagnosis in graduate counselor education. By integrating immersive storytelling, collaborative decision-making, and critical theoretical frameworks, this method enhances diagnostic reasoning, cultural responsiveness, and clinical intuition. RPGs also provide a psychologically safe structure for navigating sociopolitical pressures affecting contemporary classrooms, supporting nuanced discussions of identity, power, and systemic inequity. Through a detailed instructional model and analysis of pedagogical benefits and challenges, this paper demonstrates how RPG-based learning can strengthen diagnostic competence and prepare counselors for the complexities of modern mental health practice. (Word Count: 93)
