TY  - THES
TI  - Roll for Wellness: Tabletop Role-Playing Games and Their Impact on Social and Identity Wellness
AU  - La Brie, Melinda Jeanne
AB  - Since the 2020 COVID-19 pandemic, increases in social isolation, anxiety, identity crises, and other mental health challenges have contributed to significant changes in how people connect to each other and how they feel connected to themselves. During this time, tabletop role-playing games (TTRPGs) became more popular than ever, creating new avenues for identity exploration and social development. With a primary focus on social skills, social anxiety, loneliness, self-awareness, identity commitment, and self-esteem, a review of the literature supported not only TTRPGs’ connection to existing empirically supported interventions, but also their unique, positive impact on social and identity wellness. A quantitative study was conducted to investigate the hypotheses that TTRPG activity is positively correlated with improved symptoms of social and identity wellness, as well as anxiety and depression. A sample of 317 participants completed an online survey including demographic questions, questions about TTRPG experience, and seven psychometric instruments measuring constructs of social wellness, identity wellness, and mental health symptoms. Survey results indicated that TTRPG experience was negatively correlated with improved symptoms of most of the constructs examined. However, post-hoc analysis indicated that the majority of TTRPG players believed TTRPGs had a positive impact on their social and identity wellness. Though there were several limitations to this study, findings suggested that a significant relationship does exist between TTRPGs and social and identity wellness. Given the literature and players’ perceived positive impact of TTRPGs, a theorized explanation is that TTRPGs provide a safe and appealing form of social connection for those already experiencing social and identity related challenges. Therefore, clinicians should demonstrate increased curiosity about the clinical relevance of TTRPGs, and their role in providing refuge and growth for those experiencing threats to social and identity wellness.
