TY  - JOUR
TI  - Roll for Initiative! The case for Dungeons & Dragons-based interventions to support wellbeing for neurodivergent people
AU  - Huckfield, DA
T2  - Perspectives in Public Health
AB  - Roll for Initiative! is a Dungeons & Dragons (D&D)-based creative health intervention run at The Amelia Scott. The programme explores how tabletop role-playing games (TTRPGs) can nurture creativity, build confidence, and foster meaningful connections among adults seeking to improve mental wellbeing. Role-playing games can be transformational, offering long-term benefits – particularly for neurodivergent individuals and others who may not engage with traditional arts-based programmes. Through collaborative storytelling and imaginative play, participants form lasting social bonds and discover new ways to express themselves.
This impact is already evidenced: across two iterations – one in-person and one online – the course has supported 20 participants. This article outlines the structure of the programme and presents existing evidence supporting the effectiveness of TTRPGs as wellbeing interventions.
The Amelia Scott is a multi-functional cultural hub in Tunbridge Wells, opened in 2022 and run by Tunbridge Wells Borough Council. It is the first UK building to combine a civic museum and art gallery, library, tourist information, adult education, and council services.
