AB  - The book opens with a chapter of Introduction by the editors Frans Mäyrä and Raine Koskimaa, providing an overall framing and presenting both the aims and the outline of the entire book. The introductory chapter discusses the emergence and development of cultural game studies as a research field and as an academic discipline. It also addresses the motivation for bringing together the multiple perspectives related to different games, diverse groups of players, and their (sometimes conflicting) motivations, needs, and meaning-making processes, in addition to the need for understanding both the creation and production-related perspectives of games as a cultural industry. The multiple uses, applications, and institutional as well as informal positionalities of games and play related cultural forms in contemporary society are also covered.
