TY  - JOUR
TI  - Critical Making: Conceptual and Material Studies in Technology and Social Life
AU  - Ratto, Matt
T2  - The Information Society
AB  - And the Crops Withered (Alice D Games 2025) is a single-player tabletop roleplaying game (TTRPG) I designed, inspired by the Greek myth of “The Abduction of Persephone.” In this game, players narrate the journey of Demeter, the harvest goddess, across a world ravaged by her own divine fury to find her missing daughter. Demeter’s quest is constructed as the player draws cards from a tarot deck and matches the suit to a prompt to guide narration. This presentation covers my process for designing And the Crops Withered, in which I situate game design as what Ratto (2011) calls “critical making” and demonstrate it as a tool for mythologizing. Through this articulation, I argue that game design can enliven myths, translating them to speak to contemporary circumstances.
