TY  - THES
TI  - Telegraphed Dangers: Enemy Intercompatibility in D20-Based Fantasy OSR Tabletop Roleplaying Games
AU  - Huovila, Hiski
AB  - The OSR (Old-School Revival, Renaissance or Revolution) is a movement within the tabletop roleplaying community, focused on playing and creating games that recreate or build upon early editions of Dungeons and Dragons. This thesis studies 29 popular d20-based fantasy OSR games using qualitative document analysis, documenting which games share a possible enemy conversion between them. The OSR style is characterized by grounded and highly lethal play where simple and interpretation heavy rulesets force players to use their skill and intuition to survive. These games feature numeric representation of enemies called statblocks, which are used to efficiently convey their combat abilities. Because the movement has a shared design origin, many OSR games advertise compatibility with old-school material or each other. Compatibility has been studied on system level and attempts have been made to create standards for easy conversion but the community lacks extensive resources on the intercompatibility of these games. This study contributes such resource, documenting the prevalence of common statblock attributes (such as health, armor, and speed) and which games are compatible with each other. The study notes that while no game in the dataset is perfectly compatible with all other games in the study, it is possible to convert between many of the games with relatively simple modifications.
