TY  - THES
TI  - The Gamification of Literature : introduction to the LitRPG-genre, Role-Playing Game elements as part of storytelling
AU  - Kinnunen, Ilari
AB  - With the introduction of the first tabletop role-playing games back in 1970’s, the act of role-playing has slowly been incorporated to various other types of role-playing experiences, such as video games and books.
In the early 2010s, a new genre of literature started to gain popularity among readers of fantasy literature, called LitRPG. This new genre combined the elements of role-playing games as part of the storytelling, by incorporating various mechanics and terminology used in role-playing games. This type of literature offers a unique way of experiencing the world by explaining in detail the various systems governing the world, while following the characters progression in the story.
The goal was to introduce LitRPG as a genre and some of the other genres often associated with LitRPG, what are the elements that make up a LitRPG story and what are some of the challenges of writing this kind of literature. Another objective was to discover how some of these challenges correlate to their video-game counter parts.
The implementation method chosen was qualitative with semi- and highly structured interviews. Answers given were fully anonymous with questions tailored towards the individual industry professionals.It is concluded that LitRPGs are a new, growing genre of fantasy literature that offers a unique style of storytelling. Some of the challenges video game developers face while creating role-playing games are part of the LitRPG writing process, but they are two separate types of media with their own, unique challenges.
