TI  - STEM Learning in TTRPGs: What Is Being Assessed? How Hair Math Uses Storytelling and Play to Reimagine STEM Assessment
AU  - De La Cruz, Sharon Lee
AU  - Alimohamed, Sana
T3  - IDC '26
AB  - Hair Math is a fantasy tabletop role-playing game (TTRPG) in which players explore mathematical concepts, particularly braid theory and knot theory, through culturally grounded collaborative storytelling. This Work in Progress presents the theoretical framework and design methodology underlying Hair Math, situating the game within Freirean pedagogy and play theory to argue for narrative-based STEM learning as an alternative to assessment-driven instruction. We examine a central tension in this work: if mathematical understanding is meant to emerge through story, play, and cultural meaning-making, what is being assessed and how? Drawing on design-based research, we present an observational methodology for tracking engagement, mathematical reasoning, and affective experience during gameplay. We report on a preliminary informal pilot session with adults and describe plans for expanded testing with middle and high school students in informal learning environments.
