AB  - Roll for Reality is a live, improvised Dungeons &amp; Dragons show that combines tabletop roleplaying, improvised acting, motion capture, and real-time virtual production into a shared spatial storytelling experience. Performers seated at a physical play table collaboratively play out an epic fantasy narrative story while engaging with the digital world rendered live for audiences on a large-scale LED display. The project explores how live improvisation, tabletop roleplaying games, and real-time rendering pipelines can be unified into a single interactive storytelling medium.
