TI  - Conlangs in Video and Table-Top Gaming
AU  - Windsor, Joseph W.
T2  - The Palgrave Handbook of Constructed Languages
A2  - Windsor, Joseph W.
A2  - Long, Alison
AB  - This chapter examines how constructed languages (conlangs) are used in table-top as well as computer/video games to increase verisimilitude, shape game-play mechanics, and influence player engagement and fun. I outline a spectrum from unconscious conlanging used in inventing proper nouns for character and place names to full-fledged conlangs used by some games where the language contributes to the plot centrally, or is the purpose of the game. I consider games like specific modules of Dungeons & Dragaons such as the Tomb of Annihilation, The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim, and Dialect: A Game about Language and How It Dies to showcase this spectrum.
