TI  - AI to replace players who temporarily leave the table in online tabletop RPGs
AU  - Xin, Tong
AU  - Kimiya, Fujisawa
T2  - 2025 IEEE Cyber Science and Technology Congress (CyberSciTech)
AB  - This study presents an AI agent designed to temporarily replace absent players in online, text-based Chinese Tabletop Role-Playing Games (TRPGs). The goal is to maintain narrative continuity and improve the overall player experience. We fine-tuned large language models, including DeepSeek and ChatGPT, using five full-length TRPG session transcripts (3–8 hours each), enabling the AI to mimic player dialogue and in-character behavior. The agent supports basic interactions and helps sustain game flow during player absences. While the system performs well in conversational contexts, it currently struggles with generating longer descriptive texts, which are important for immersive storytelling. This ongoing research aims to enhance accessibility and fluidity in distributed TRPG play through adaptive language model integration.
