TI  - “This mess my fault?”: Cyberpsychosis and late-capitalist real subsumption in Cyberpunk 2020, Cyberpunk 2077, and Edgerunners
AU  - Shipko, David
T2  - Science Fiction Film & Television
AB  - This article examines the construction and function of the cyberpsychosis novum as developed within the Cyberpunk franchise, specifically the tabletop role-playing game Cyberpunk 2020 (1988), the role-playing videogame Cyberpunk 2077 (2020), and the anime series Cyberpunk: Edgerunners (2022). Situating these texts within the historical context of “chatbot psychosis” and other subjective consequences of the proliferation of so-called “artificial intelligence” technologies, this article explores how these Cyberpunk texts use cyberpsychosis, the event of the cyberpsychotic break, and the figure of the cyberpsycho to mediate the conditions and contradictions of late-capitalist real subsumption.
