TI  - Choosing our own adventures: Reflections on hosting digital fiction game jams and workshops in an academic library
AU  - Post, Colin
AU  - Aliu, Xhenet
AU  - Birkner, Charlie
AU  - Plemmons, Callie
AU  - Bowman, Katie
T2  - College & Undergraduate Libraries
AB  - Academic libraries have recognized the value of promoting digital creativity, though limited research has been conducted on game design activities in libraries. Similarly, creative writing educators have increasingly integrated game design tools and approaches into the classroom, but there has been little discussion on how libraries can supplement this curriculum. To explore these topics, we ran two digital fiction game jams, events where students created and shared original narrative games in a university library media lab. We found the library in our case study to be a conducive space for providing students with the resources and technologies to advance their skills in creating and sharing narrative games.
