AU  - Deiorio, Nicole M.
AU  - Moberly, Richard
AU  - Schneider, Benjamin
T2  - Journal of Graduate Medical Education
AB  - “Welcome! Today you begin your quest to choose your intern class.”

The Medical Student Performance Evaluation (MSPE), a cornerstone of residency applications, is in desperate need of redesign.1 The intent is good: to provide a quick, standardized way for program directors to efficiently compare applicants. But arguably the most valued and unique features—the “at-a-glance” core clerkship grade distribution graphs and the summary statement describing class rank—are norm-based and thus increasingly at odds with the principles of competency-based medical education.2 With the Association of American Medical Colleges (AAMC)-Thalamus collaboration, and the 2026 Match season launch of the Cortex holistic review platform,3 MSPE class distributions may become redundant since these data can be extracted from transcripts using artificial intelligence.
