AU  - Lenets, Anna Viktorovna
T2  - Bulletin of the Donetsk National University. Series D: Philology and Psychology
AB  - The article deals with mythonyms as linguo‑semiotic means of verbalizing virtual worlds within the English‑language tabletop role‑playing game (TRPG) discourse. The relevance of the study is accounted for by the growing role of neo‑mythological structures in contemporary culture and a lack of integrated approaches to analyzing mythonyms in gaming discourse. The study is aimed at identifying the typological features of mythonyms and at determining their role in constructing a secondary mythological reality. The research material comprises the texts of English‑language cyberpunk tabletop role‑playing games (“Cyberpunk 2020”, “Cyberpunk RED”, “Neotribes”), from which 280 mythonymic units were extracted via continuous sampling. The contextual, pragmatic, and linguosemiotic methods of analysis have been applied. The findings indicate that mythonyms possess high semiotic density, perform symbolic, culturally marked, and precedent functions, and serve as a key tool for constructing a cohesive semiotic game space.
