TY  - JOUR
TI  - RPG-Based Gamification in Teaching Modern Physics
AU  - Herendi, Borbála
AU  - Varga, Szabolcs
AU  - Jenei, Péter
T2  - The Physics Teacher
AB  - Students nowadays spend hundreds of hours playing role-playing game (RPG)-based video games. The system of these games attracts them; hence, it might be worth a try in education. Classcraft Learning Management System (LMS) builds on this natural interest, which, like in RPG characters, can be built and developed through learning. In this study, a part of modern physics (special relativity, blackbody radiation, photoelectric effect, atomic models, and wave–particle duality) was taught using this LMS. Half of one class was taught using traditional methods (control group), and the other half used Classcraft (experimental group). The classroom work has not been substantially modified; our aim was to find out whether the attitude of the students toward doing their homework and participating in class improved. We found that the experimental group put more effort into their learning, and thus, their knowledge improved more than that of the control group from the pretest to the posttest. Furthermore, the students were more passionate about using this learning method.
