TY  - JOUR
TI  - Tabletop Role-Playing Games as a Tool for Adults
AU  - Sinning, Amy
AB  - One way to assist people in re-building their identity is to allow them to explore identity in a safe environment. Identity issues can develop for a variety of reasons, including changing of career. Whether, voluntary or forced, a change in career can be a life altering event. There has been no systematic investigations exploring how roleplaying games have been used in therapy with adults so far. Tabletop Role-Playing Games (TTRPG) haves been used in the therapy space, as a way for people to explore identity, personal issues or problems in a low risk and safe setting. This has been mainly used with children and adolescents in a therapeutic setting. However recently, the use of TTRPG in adult populations is finding just as much success as with children.
This review aims to understand how TTRPGs are being used in adult populations. This scoping review will map the existing literature of tabletop roleplaying games used in therapy interventions designed to promote mental health and prevent mental health problems. This scoping review will clarify the content and characteristics of which interventions and will describe the theoretical models and relevant outcome measures used in the studies.
