TI  - Supplementary Material for "The AI Player as Narrative Design Partner: Exploring AI Participation in Tabletop Role-Playing Games"
AU  - Sakellariadis, Pantelis
AU  - Katifori, Akrivi
AU  - Petousi, Dimitra
AU  - Koutiva, Georgia
AU  - Ioannidis, Yannis
AB  - This supplementary material accompanies the paper "The AI Player as Narrative Design Partner: Exploring AI Participation in Tabletop Role-Playing Games" (presented at the 19th International Conference on Interactive Digital Storytelling). It provides qualitative materials and documentation from the study, structured into three main sections:



AI Player Initialization Prompt: Outlines the structured prompt used to initialize the AI model as an experienced tabletop RPG player participating in a custom D&D 5e campaign, covering player persona, role-playing expectations, collaborative character creation, communication protocols, reflection practices, and world context.

Gameplay Excerpts: Features real interaction transcripts between the human Game Master (GM) and the AI player (character Ilintha) as they navigate narrative decisions, stealth, and key plot points.

Player Reflection: A post-game interview capturing reflections on character growth, emotional resonance, narrative turning points, the DM-player dynamic, and the overall immersion of collaborative storytelling.
